@chapter 9 | Nuclear Physics

@intro
Nuclear questions fall into three groups: **physics** (fission and fusion, the Sun's energy, atom bomb vs hydrogen bomb vs reactor, discoverers of particles), **reactor technology** (fuel, enrichment, **moderators and coolants**, breeder reactors, heavy water) and **India's nuclear map** (Tarapur to Kudankulam, Kalpakkam and the three-stage programme with **thorium**, research reactors, and the Pokhran tests). It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 9.1 | Discoveries and Basic Ideas

@src 11:1
@pyq U.P. P.C.S. (Pre) 2001, 2003; U.P. U.D.A./L.D.A. (Pre) 2002
Which one of the following pairs is not correctly matched :
(a) Discovery of Meson – Hideki Yukawa
(b) Discovery of Positron – C.D. Anderson and U.F. Hess
(c) Theory of energy production in the sun and stars – H.A. Bethe
(d) Synthesis of transuranic elements – Enrico Fermi
@ans (d)
@end

**Yukawa** predicted the meson (1935); **Anderson** found the positron (1932) and shared the 1936 Nobel with **Hess**, the discoverer of cosmic rays; **Bethe** explained stellar fusion (1938-39). The transuranium elements (beyond uranium) were made mainly by **Glenn Seaborg**'s team, although Fermi's 1934 neutron experiments started the search.

