@section 9.6 | Nuclear Tests and Security

@q 11:39

@src 11:41
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 1999
'Operation Shakti'-98 is the name :
(a) Given to the nuclear test carried out at Pokharan in 1998
(b) Given to air exercises carried out by Indian Air Force SU-30 planes
(c) Given to the pro-active programme of the Union Home Minister to contain terrorism in J& K
(d) Given to military action against terrorists in Tripura
@ans (a)
@end

India's first test, **Smiling Buddha** (Pokhran-I), was on **18 May 1974**. **Operation Shakti** (Pokhran-II) was five tests on **11 and 13 May 1998**; 11 May is celebrated as **National Technology Day**. India follows **no first use** and a voluntary test moratorium.

@q 11:40

@trap
**Fission splits, fusion joins.** The **Sun** runs on **hydrogen → helium** fusion. **Atom bomb = fission, H-bomb = fusion**, reactor = **controlled** fission. Moderators **slow** neutrons (heavy water, graphite); control rods **absorb** them (boron, cadmium). Fast breeders use **liquid sodium**. **Harish-Chandra Research Institute is in Prayagraj**, not Chennai. **Kudankulam** has the highest capacity; **Narora** is in zone IV.
@end

